 {"id":"fabro-37a6","title":"Steer implementer to mechanical shell bulk edits for repetitive rewrites","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-04T23:01:45.209Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T09:47:52.651Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, add one paragraph: for repetitive, pattern-shaped changes (call-site adaptation, renames), do one mechanical pass via shell (sd/perl -pi -e, already pinned in the runner image) and verify with one focused test, instead of N hand edits. Evidence: implementer@2 (fabro-28e8) was 42% of run cost ($0.486, 278s, 51.8k tokens) rewriting ~24 identical call sites one edit_file at a time, with 19 concurrent-write serialization warnings across passes and one swallowed-loop-body near-miss. Expected effect: refactor-class pass drops from ~$0.49/280s toward ~$0.12/112s; run cost -20-25%; eliminates the swallow-adjacent-code near-miss class. Distinct from fabro-4601 (sequential-edit discipline, different mechanism).","labels":["revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T09:47:52.651Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-d5a6","title":"web: files tab refuses large diffs ('too large to render inline') — offer truncated/per-record rendering","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:35.110Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:35.110Z","description":"User report 2026-09-05: in a run's Files tab, the diff for .seeds/issues.jsonl (182 records / ~264KB) is refused with '.seeds/issues.jsonl too large to render inline', so revisor-filed seeds cannot be reviewed in the UI at all. Wanted: at minimum a truncated diff with explicit cut + full-diff download; ideally per-record (JSONL line) diff rendering so one revisor cycle's additions are readable. Basis: revisor run on denkhaus, Files tab, 2026-09-05.","labels":["web","ux"]}
 {"id":"fabro-71b9","title":"web: kanban run tiles — show run date, workflow name, and workflow version","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T08:41:02.820Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T08:41:02.820Z","description":"User request 2026-09-05: the kanban run tiles currently show only title, diff status, repo, and PR numbers. Wanted additionally on each tile: (1) the run date (created_at or last activity), (2) the workflow name, (3) the workflow version. The workflow_version_id is content-derived (SHA-256 of the canonical workflow package) and exposed by the API run record as workflow.workflow_version_id (runs list since ADR-0015 engine change, 2026-09-05); render a short form (first ~12 hex chars) so tiles stay compact. Complements fabro-d5a6 (large-diff rendering); together they close the run-identity visibility gap in the UI.","labels":["web","ux","workflows"]}
-{"id":"fabro-56c2","title":"State the fs_hide shell bypass plainly in develop prompts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T09:56:55.646Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T09:56:55.646Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md (Platform scope section) and prompts/planner.md (ADR-0015 stale-basis step), replace the claim 'writes are denied (fabro-1dae fs_hide)' — disproved in the target run — with explicit guidance that for platform-targeting seeds, .fabro/** reads/writes go through the shell because fs_hide binds tool calls only (implementer read_file denied at seq 145, then 3 discovery calls before a python3 heredoc edit at seq 174; planner forced into shell fallback at seq 83). Effect: 3-4 tool calls and 2-3 LLM turns saved per platform-targeting seed, and prompts stop asserting unenforced behavior. Basis: run 01M1RF53QWM4Q5REBVSG9F9Y43, workflow version absent, commit 3ca43b1cd19c8cf291668bdbdc4a1fbbc321e2ec","labels":["revision"]}
